###  https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core#TextileApparel
:TextileApparel rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:subClassOf :TextileProduct ;
                <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf> ;
                rdfs:comment "Textile products that aim to cover the body with everything except footwear, including clothing and clothing accessories worn to clothe, adorn, shield, provide comfort, or express identity and belonging."@en ;
                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core> ;
                rdfs:label "Textile apparel"@en ;
                <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "TextileApparel is a final textile product category for apparel and apparel accessories. The supplied EU DPP Core snapshot does not declare a separate FinalProduct class, so final-product status remains a local textile distinction under dpp:Product. It is narrower than TextileProduct and should not be confused with the whole textile product domain."@en ;
                <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceLocator> "JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, printed page 14, lines 167-170; JRC Preparatory Study, Section 3.2.1, printed pages 24-25, lines 443-468; JRC Preparatory Study, Section 3.2.1, Table 7, printed page 24; caption line 450."@en ;
                <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceType> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#adaptedDefinition> ;
                :defaultStudyScopeStatus <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-codelists#includedInJRCPreparatoryStudyScope> .


